  "source_safety": {
    "input_pixels": "<=12logical values in these recipes (32 source-safe specifications); stepped backing<=24elements, sum of encoded owner/view arrays bounded192. All integer values representable in declared dtype.",
    "ordinary_morphology": "Positive nonempty integer/bool arrays rank1..4, footprint3^rank<=81, source reflect radius1; no custom footprints/protocols/NaN/uncheckedshortshape. SciPy morphology supports the standard rank/shape arguments; no raw fabricated buffers.",
    "subpixel": "Expanded extents2*s-1, ordinary output<=25positions; np.pad adds1edge border, 3^rank rolling windows stay within padded owned array. Dtype-max collision preserved exactly. Zero-axis case raises at source np.zeros negative extent before view_as_windows.",
    "errors": "List lacksdtype before any footprint/filter; connectivityNone fails its pure-Python comparison before footprint/filter; empty-subpixel negative allocation before rolling windows. Record actual errors, do not synthesize messages.",
    "shape_dtype_order": "Ordinary result comes from source empty_like/minmax/ufunc allocation, potentially K/F/permuted order. Captures must preserve this; no assumed C-only result. Subpixel uses source zeros_like Cexpanded buffer.",
    "integer_semantics": "SciPy min/max converts typed inputs to double, chooses extrema, casts back at every pass. All ordinary int8/16/32/u8/u16/u32 values AND generated dtype maxima are exact in double and cast-safe. Ordinary i64 thick control uses only [2^53,2^53+2], rounds nonexact2^53+1 but every rounded double remains in int64 range. No ordinary int64/u64 outer recipe: even low input labels may create unsafe dtype-max sentinels before erosion. Full-width uint64-max is retained ONLY in subpixel, whose integer unique/comparison path bypasses ndimage."
  },
